  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Kerala High Court has recently presided over a diverse array of legal matters involving political, educational, and corruption-related disputes. In criminal law, a court convicted three BJP-RSS members for the 2016 killing of a local CPI(M) leader. Simultaneously, the court is reviewing an appeal from Sree Sankaracharya University of Sanskrit (SSUS) concerning the suspension of 16 students associated with the Students’ Federation of India; the university argues that upholding a lower court's decision to revoke these suspensions could lead to institutional disorder. Judicial oversight continues in multiple corruption cases, with the court recently disposing of a plea regarding an FIR against Ramesh Chennithala and extending a stay on the investigation involving Chief Minister Pinarayi Vijayan and his family in the CMRL-Exalogic payoff case. Additionally, the court addressed procedures regarding the state Waqf Board and investigations into the SNDP microfinance scam.",
